answer	std::map does ~log2 N dependent pointer chases to scattered heap nodes (cache misses at large N). flat_map searches one array whose top probe levels stay cache-hot, with no node overhead. A hash table does O(1) expected probes rather than ~log2 N; boost::unordered_flat_map won every point-lookup row measured.
